model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-05-10
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  note "T, tally 2.1.8 R12 (#196), no-item 6: an entry K + [k] lives … known in a window that holds the cut: count(x in K on d) is the hole (c), windows each gives the two counts (c_each); before and after the window it answers (c_before, c_after)"

source s "s"
kind persons

version v1
  cite s
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ola] lives 1990-02-01..

version v2
  cite s
  known window(2026-04-01, 2026-04-20)
  persons + [jan] lives 1991-02-01..

ask c: count(p in persons on 2026-03-01) as known 2026-04-10
ask c_each: count(p in persons on 2026-03-01) as known 2026-04-10 windows each
ask c_before: count(p in persons on 2026-03-01) as known 2026-03-31
ask c_after: count(p in persons on 2026-03-01) as known 2026-04-21
